 "result_text": "`checkout_github_prs()` no longer fails when the `--all`, `--mine` or `--by` criteria match no open PRs. It now prints a warning and returns without fetching or changing anything. I didn't run the tests or try it against GitHub.\n\nThe change is in `git_machete/client.py`. `__get_valid_pull_requests` used to raise a `MacheteException` in those three cases. It now warns and returns an empty list. `checkout_github_prs` returns early when that list is empty.\n\nI left explicit PR numbers alone. If you ask for specific PR numbers and none are found, it still raises an error. The issue talks about \"criteria\", so I read it as covering only the `--all`/`--mine`/`--by` filters. Say so if you want the explicit-number case to warn instead.",
